1
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:03,092
Guys, I have great news!

2
00:00:03,117 --> 00:00:05,797
We made a huge profit
at Bake Haus of U today!

3
00:00:06,357 --> 00:00:07,910
- Wow!
- Wow!

4
00:00:08,137 --> 00:00:09,043
Awesome, right?

5
00:00:09,068 --> 00:00:11,205
We’ve got a new
branding now—we’re rich!

6
00:00:12,731 --> 00:00:13,958
Since we’re on topic,

7
00:00:14,621 --> 00:00:16,248
I’m happy to announce that.

8
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:19,394
SpaKarl’s social media
page is finally doing well!

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,933
The likes, views, and of course…

10
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:23,686
Comments!

11
00:00:23,711 --> 00:00:27,636
I’m so proud of you
two, you’re both amazing!

12
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,240
No, and you know what,

13
00:00:30,743 --> 00:00:34,329
BFF has really been a big help to us!

14
00:00:34,354 --> 00:00:38,270
Just think about it—he
gave way for our bakery,

15
00:00:38,518 --> 00:00:41,232
and even gave Andres a job.

16
00:00:41,335 --> 00:00:45,661
I hope nothing changes.

17
00:00:46,049 --> 00:00:48,822
I mean, our business has
been around for a while.

18
00:00:48,847 --> 00:00:51,518
Hopefully, it keeps going strong.

19
00:00:51,919 --> 00:00:52,932
Exactly!

20
00:00:53,323 --> 00:00:56,476
You know, we’ve really
been at this a long time.

21
00:00:56,713 --> 00:01:00,426
So much has happened here...

22
00:01:00,543 --> 00:01:02,677
it’s got a long history.

23
00:01:03,353 --> 00:01:06,273
That reminds me of
your Grandpa Roman.

24
00:01:06,413 --> 00:01:08,999
A lot of things
happened here back

25
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:10,876
when it was just the two of us.

26
00:01:11,742 --> 00:01:14,742
Then he locked the door,

27
00:01:14,895 --> 00:01:18,740
and I was so shocked because
suddenly, he got down on one knee!

28
00:01:18,765 --> 00:01:22,164
- Lola Maxi!
- Then he suddenly put it in!

29
00:01:22,189 --> 00:01:23,479
Lola Maxi!

30
00:01:24,006 --> 00:01:24,439
What?

31
00:01:24,464 --> 00:01:25,465
We’re eating!

32
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,314
So? What did I even say?

33
00:01:27,339 --> 00:01:29,542
That’s so gross,
what you’re saying!

34
00:01:30,055 --> 00:01:31,835
Ross? Love is gross to you now?

35
00:01:32,011 --> 00:01:35,532
Oh, come on! That’s the
problem with you kids...

36
00:01:35,557 --> 00:01:38,143
you always jump
to dirty thoughts!

37
00:01:38,168 --> 00:01:40,741
I was just talking about when

38
00:01:40,927 --> 00:01:48,104
Roman proposed to me, and
he put the ring on my finger!

39
00:01:49,832 --> 00:01:51,272
You should’ve let me finish first!

40
00:01:51,297 --> 00:01:53,368
- Gosh, Lola Maxi!
- She’s right.

41
00:02:54,278 --> 00:02:55,718
What happened to those two?

42
00:02:59,802 --> 00:03:00,608
Hey, you witch!

43
00:03:00,683 --> 00:03:01,683
Come here!

44
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:03,530
Let’s start a fight.

45
00:03:03,748 --> 00:03:05,041
Why? What for?

46
00:03:05,066 --> 00:03:05,629
What happened?

47
00:03:05,654 --> 00:03:09,033
Because it’s been too peaceful
here in Barangay Singko lately.

48
00:03:09,248 --> 00:03:11,407
No fights, no juicy gossip.

49
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:15,132
Look at our gossip
queens—they're fading!

50
00:03:15,157 --> 00:03:17,918
They’ve got nothing to talk
about, no source of vitamin C!

51
00:03:18,232 --> 00:03:21,819
You know what, that’s actually
a good thing—it’s peaceful!

52
00:03:22,041 --> 00:03:23,681
Careful what you wish for,

53
00:03:23,706 --> 00:03:26,510
someone might actually come
stir up trouble in Barangay Singko!

54
00:03:32,401 --> 00:03:33,608
- Excuse me!
- What now, just let it be...

55
00:03:33,632 --> 00:03:34,632
- Oh…
- Oh…

56
00:03:39,785 --> 00:03:43,138
Hello, excuse me,
who are you looking for?

57
00:03:44,764 --> 00:03:45,764
Huh?

58
00:03:46,045 --> 00:03:49,552
Oh, I’m looking for the part
of me that cares about you!

59
00:03:49,709 --> 00:03:52,622
Whoa, that’s harsh!

60
00:03:52,647 --> 00:03:54,642
We just want to help, miss!

61
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:58,291
Well, you did help—help
raise my blood pressure!

62
00:03:59,813 --> 00:04:01,013
She’s something else.

63
00:04:01,038 --> 00:04:04,287
Cut it out! You want me to
shave the hair off your nose too?

64
00:04:04,312 --> 00:04:05,987
Hey, she knows you're bald!

65
00:04:06,012 --> 00:04:07,081
Hey! How did you know I’m bald?!

66
00:04:07,105 --> 00:04:08,722
I know a lot about you!

67
00:04:08,868 --> 00:04:09,862
Get out of here!

68
00:04:09,887 --> 00:04:10,825
Should I start listing
them one by one?!

69
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:13,813
Get out! You’re a Cup
D, I know you’re a Cup D!

70
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:15,953
Used to be a cup…
now it’s the World Cup!

71
00:04:16,495 --> 00:04:19,642
Get off my case,
ugh! I’m so pissed!

72
00:04:19,893 --> 00:04:22,020
See? It came true!

73
00:04:22,286 --> 00:04:24,186
- Who do you think that is?
- There she is!

74
00:04:24,872 --> 00:04:25,872
Oh!

75
00:04:26,318 --> 00:04:27,318
The energy just shifted!

76
00:04:27,493 --> 00:04:28,587
Suddenly…

77
00:04:29,053 --> 00:04:30,293
- They’re alive!
- They’re back!

78
00:04:31,297 --> 00:04:32,997
Wow, all it takes is some gossip!

79
00:04:33,296 --> 00:04:34,525
- Amazing!
- Got their vitamins!

80
00:04:34,549 --> 00:04:35,549
Look at them go!

81
00:04:43,442 --> 00:04:46,855
Hey, you two!
Back to work, okay?

82
00:04:46,955 --> 00:04:47,947
Hold on, Tash.

83
00:04:47,972 --> 00:04:50,065
People are just on break.

84
00:04:50,371 --> 00:04:51,538
We’re super tired.

85
00:04:51,563 --> 00:04:52,563
Break?

86
00:04:52,801 --> 00:04:55,175
Hello, your break is over.

87
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,227
Sorry.

88
00:04:56,305 --> 00:04:57,145
Oh, sorry, Ma’am…

89
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:59,837
- Okay.
- Wow, Tash, you’re too much.

90
00:04:59,916 --> 00:05:02,277
You’re so strict,
like a dictator.

91
00:05:02,396 --> 00:05:05,390
Hey, I’m not a dictator.

92
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,737
Just do your job properly...

93
00:05:07,832 --> 00:05:09,579
or else, I will fire you both!

94
00:05:09,604 --> 00:05:11,652
- Whoa, don’t be like that!
- Okay, okay, okay!

95
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,843
- I just dozed off for a sec.
- Don’t be like that, Tash.

96
00:05:19,087 --> 00:05:20,087
Hey…

97
00:05:21,382 --> 00:05:22,575
Oh…well that woke me up.

98
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,800
Wow, it’s almost Christmas.
Look, there’s queso de bola!

99
00:05:26,022 --> 00:05:27,767
Queso de bola? I got this.

100
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,930
No, I got it. I’ll take care of it.

101
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:30,697
I said, I got it!

102
00:05:30,722 --> 00:05:31,837
- No, me!
- Hey!

103
00:05:31,862 --> 00:05:32,862
- Me.
- No, me!

104
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:34,580
Hi, Ma’am!

105
00:05:34,971 --> 00:05:36,131
What’s your order?

106
00:05:37,548 --> 00:05:38,548
Ooh!

107
00:05:40,972 --> 00:05:42,018
- Order?
- Yes!

108
00:05:42,111 --> 00:05:45,331
Oh, order…deodorant!

109
00:05:45,670 --> 00:05:46,577
- Deodorant?
- Mm-hmm.

110
00:05:46,602 --> 00:05:48,916
One each for the two
of you—you both stink!

111
00:05:50,813 --> 00:05:51,553
You go.

112
00:05:51,578 --> 00:05:52,786
You go, you’re already there.

113
00:05:52,963 --> 00:05:53,423
You go.

114
00:05:53,461 --> 00:05:55,520
- You’re already in front, you go.
- Fine, I’ll go!

115
00:05:55,698 --> 00:05:57,258
- You…
- Miss, what are you looking for?

116
00:05:58,282 --> 00:05:59,982
Uh, what I’m looking for?

117
00:06:00,007 --> 00:06:00,629
Yes!

118
00:06:00,654 --> 00:06:05,729
Oh, okay… I’m looking
for my uncle’s bakeshop.

119
00:06:05,848 --> 00:06:06,849
Yeah, that’s what
I’m looking for.

120
00:06:06,873 --> 00:06:11,434
But I’m pretty sure this
isn’t it… looks kinda cheap.

121
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,380
Oh really?

122
00:06:26,259 --> 00:06:29,423
You’re looking down
on me and my shop?

123
00:06:29,756 --> 00:06:30,890
Remember this...

124
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:35,141
something small like this
could still poke you in the eye.

125
00:06:36,922 --> 00:06:37,922
Poke me?

126
00:06:39,343 --> 00:06:40,610
Then I’ll wear shades.

127
00:06:42,365 --> 00:06:43,505
You know what, I like you.

128
00:06:43,886 --> 00:06:45,900
You’re fierce like me.

129
00:06:48,165 --> 00:06:49,165
I’m Hannah.

130
00:06:49,827 --> 00:06:50,827
I’m Tash.

131
00:06:51,091 --> 00:06:52,645
I bet you’re looking for Tso K...

132
00:06:52,835 --> 00:06:54,095
the stale bakery?

133
00:06:54,641 --> 00:06:55,841
It’s right there, on the side.

134
00:06:56,058 --> 00:06:58,723
Just be careful, the place is gross.

135
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:02,982
That’s fine, I’m on my
way anyway. I’m gorgeous.

136
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:06,260
Excuse me.

137
00:07:17,116 --> 00:07:21,562
And that was the first
meeting of two rivals.

138
00:07:22,395 --> 00:07:25,986
Stay tuned to see what happens next

139
00:07:26,331 --> 00:07:32,310
in the next episode of
Hannah versus Tasha.

140
00:07:36,402 --> 00:07:38,695
Anne, are you coin changes?

141
00:07:38,768 --> 00:07:39,768
Why?

142
00:07:40,249 --> 00:07:43,836
Ecause even this early
in the morning—I need you.

143
00:07:44,604 --> 00:07:47,969
Ou’re too much! You’re
making me blush!

144
00:07:49,156 --> 00:07:50,010
Andres…

145
00:07:50,096 --> 00:07:51,682
- What?
- Are you a ghost?

146
00:07:52,255 --> 00:07:53,055
Why?

147
00:07:53,275 --> 00:07:55,881
Because I’m haunted by you!

148
00:07:58,297 --> 00:07:59,337
You know what, Anne,

149
00:08:00,887 --> 00:08:04,022
when I first saw
you—I totally lost power.

150
00:08:04,483 --> 00:08:05,483
Why?

151
00:08:06,202 --> 00:08:07,302
Well, obviously…

152
00:08:08,243 --> 00:08:09,910
it was low-batt at first sight!

153
00:08:14,392 --> 00:08:15,926
Andres, don’t you have work?

154
00:08:16,965 --> 00:08:17,965
W-why?

155
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:19,463
What do you mean why?

156
00:08:19,488 --> 00:08:21,997
Aren’t you supposed to
be working at SpaKarl?

157
00:08:22,062 --> 00:08:23,231
What are you doing here?

158
00:08:23,543 --> 00:08:26,183
Well, a battery needs
to recharge, right?

159
00:08:26,208 --> 00:08:27,092
Oh?

160
00:08:27,149 --> 00:08:29,469
So, I’m recharging here.

161
00:08:29,569 --> 00:08:30,072
Huh?

162
00:08:30,097 --> 00:08:31,177
- Yep.
- How?

163
00:08:31,836 --> 00:08:34,763
Well… kiss me.

164
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:38,475
Fine!

165
00:08:41,363 --> 00:08:42,363
Hey!

166
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:47,890
Hey… what’s that?!

167
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:49,152
“What’s that?”

168
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:52,138
You’re interrupting something!

169
00:08:52,964 --> 00:08:54,064
Buy your stuff later!

170
00:09:02,095 --> 00:09:03,225
I am so mad right now!

171
00:09:05,761 --> 00:09:06,761
Hannah!

172
00:09:07,717 --> 00:09:11,324
Hannah, my niece!

173
00:09:12,914 --> 00:09:14,574
Ate Hannah?!

174
00:09:18,626 --> 00:09:21,921
Why are you here in Manila?!

175
00:09:22,316 --> 00:09:24,009
Last time we talked,

176
00:09:24,235 --> 00:09:25,697
you were still in the province!

177
00:09:25,722 --> 00:09:26,722
Where?!

178
00:09:27,155 --> 00:09:28,155
The province?

179
00:09:28,414 --> 00:09:29,321
Why?

180
00:09:29,384 --> 00:09:35,770
Is it bad to surprise my baby sister?

181
00:09:36,891 --> 00:09:38,238
Ah…th-that’s your older sister?

182
00:09:40,442 --> 00:09:42,155
Didn’t recognize her at first.

183
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:44,190
She changed a lot.

184
00:09:44,445 --> 00:09:45,638
A big change, yeah.

185
00:09:45,813 --> 00:09:48,233
She had no choice—I’m
her sister. Why?

186
00:09:51,931 --> 00:09:54,777
Tso K, what happened
to your bakery?

187
00:09:55,490 --> 00:09:57,097
Last time we talked, you said

188
00:09:57,122 --> 00:09:59,483
you were going to take
down all your competitors here.

189
00:09:59,536 --> 00:10:00,936
Well, nephew,

190
00:10:01,306 --> 00:10:03,440
I focused on SpaKarl,

191
00:10:04,034 --> 00:10:07,061
so I left everything
else to my BFF Aga.

192
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:08,398
Aga?

193
00:10:08,555 --> 00:10:12,641
Isn’t he the same BFF
who stole your crush before?

194
00:10:12,827 --> 00:10:15,534
Yes, but we already
patched things up.

195
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,533
Just like that?
Just like that, Tso?

196
00:10:17,786 --> 00:10:19,226
Yeah. That’s right.

197
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,547
Wait, how did we make up?

198
00:10:28,024 --> 00:10:29,024
Tso K,

199
00:10:31,592 --> 00:10:35,459
do you know why you're
my favorite uncle?

200
00:10:36,697 --> 00:10:39,825
Hmm? Because you're a fighter.

201
00:10:40,408 --> 00:10:42,855
I always remember you

202
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:47,435
whenever I take down
anyone who mocked me,

203
00:10:47,792 --> 00:10:49,786
insulted me,

204
00:10:50,392 --> 00:10:52,792
made me feel small...

205
00:10:53,365 --> 00:10:54,811
you’re the one
who comes to mind!

206
00:10:55,068 --> 00:10:58,655
Being soft doesn’t
run in our blood!

207
00:11:00,467 --> 00:11:01,467
You’re right!

208
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:04,395
You’re right… I did go soft.

209
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:07,277
Tso K, don’t worry.

210
00:11:07,898 --> 00:11:09,471
Now that I’m here in Manila,

211
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:13,617
I’ll help you with
your bakery business...

212
00:11:13,807 --> 00:11:16,207
so little by little,

213
00:11:16,255 --> 00:11:22,367
you can finally taste the
sweetness of revenge!

214
00:11:29,456 --> 00:11:30,842
- You’re right, nephew!
- Yes!

215
00:11:30,872 --> 00:11:33,717
Just wait till I see
that Aga again…

216
00:11:33,751 --> 00:11:34,355
Yes.

217
00:11:34,379 --> 00:11:35,840
Here’s what I’ll do.

218
00:11:44,345 --> 00:11:47,906
Andres, can we not see
each other for a while?

219
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,220
Why?

220
00:11:49,575 --> 00:11:51,015
Is it because of
your sister, Hannah?

221
00:11:51,221 --> 00:11:52,427
Is she that strict?

222
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,927
She’s really strict!

223
00:11:55,086 --> 00:11:56,146
Grew up on soap operas,

224
00:11:56,171 --> 00:11:58,055
and she brings all
that drama into real life!

225
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:01,530
- Oh!
- No wonder!

226
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,600
So that’s the reason!

227
00:12:02,651 --> 00:12:03,904
So I’m sorry, Andres,

228
00:12:04,486 --> 00:12:06,659
I don’t think I can
accept this right now.

229
00:12:07,502 --> 00:12:11,954
Well, that’s okay, Anne,
because this isn’t for you.

230
00:12:11,979 --> 00:12:12,474
What?!

231
00:12:12,499 --> 00:12:15,538
Excuse me?! That was fast!

232
00:12:16,009 --> 00:12:18,222
You're giving up already, Andres?!

233
00:12:18,247 --> 00:12:21,121
You're the worst!

234
00:12:21,594 --> 00:12:24,665
What I mean is—it’s
for my sister, Hannah.

235
00:12:26,130 --> 00:12:27,130
For Hannah?!

236
00:12:27,757 --> 00:12:29,377
You're giving that to Hannah?!

237
00:12:29,825 --> 00:12:30,872
Unbelievable.

238
00:12:30,897 --> 00:12:31,822
You are so awful!

239
00:12:31,847 --> 00:12:36,528
You’re the worst…

240
00:12:36,553 --> 00:12:37,553
Come on,

241
00:12:37,746 --> 00:12:43,055
I’m giving it to her because
I want to win her over.

242
00:12:43,116 --> 00:12:44,763
I need her to approve of me.

243
00:12:44,951 --> 00:12:47,018
That’s why it’s for her.

244
00:12:47,043 --> 00:12:48,635
- Oh!
- Ah!

245
00:12:48,903 --> 00:12:50,978
- You should’ve said so right away—
- Yeah, that’s all it is!

246
00:12:51,002 --> 00:12:53,399
You’re just so
dramatic—so dramatic.

247
00:12:53,424 --> 00:12:54,584
Look who’s talking!

248
00:12:54,868 --> 00:12:56,422
- Don’t be so judgmental!
- You!

249
00:12:56,535 --> 00:12:57,535
Ahem!

250
00:13:00,498 --> 00:13:01,478
Ate Hannah…

251
00:13:01,503 --> 00:13:02,257
Hannah.

252
00:13:02,282 --> 00:13:05,145
Didn’t I tell you to stay
away from my sister?

253
00:13:07,973 --> 00:13:10,073
Don’t you get it?

254
00:13:10,255 --> 00:13:13,001
He’s the son of Tso K’s mortal enemy,

255
00:13:13,576 --> 00:13:15,262
and you gave in to that?

256
00:13:15,287 --> 00:13:15,975
You’re in trouble,
I’m telling you!

257
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,540
- Ate Hannah!
- What?!

258
00:13:18,426 --> 00:13:19,426
This is for you.

259
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:21,674
Yes…

260
00:13:21,929 --> 00:13:22,609
Flowers?!

261
00:13:22,634 --> 00:13:23,634
Yes…

262
00:13:25,961 --> 00:13:26,961
Why?

263
00:13:27,087 --> 00:13:28,002
Why?

264
00:13:28,027 --> 00:13:29,434
I’m allergic to pollen!

265
00:13:29,467 --> 00:13:30,754
Oh, allergic!

266
00:13:30,779 --> 00:13:33,912
- Give it to me! Hey!
- Oh, thank you so much!

267
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:37,267
Here, take this
instead! Chocolates…

268
00:13:37,607 --> 00:13:38,760
Chocolates?

269
00:13:38,785 --> 00:13:40,160
- Chocolates.
- Yes…

270
00:13:41,032 --> 00:13:42,032
Try it, try it.

271
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,180
- Wow, it’s good!
- So good!

272
00:13:47,492 --> 00:13:50,255
Oh, oh?! What’s happening?

273
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:53,317
- What’s going on?
- Water! Water! Water!

274
00:13:53,828 --> 00:13:54,828
What’s wrong with you?

275
00:13:55,425 --> 00:13:56,659
You’ve taken this way too far!

276
00:13:57,505 --> 00:13:58,505
It has nuts!

277
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,453
I’m allergic to nuts!

278
00:14:00,478 --> 00:14:01,864
Milk tea, milk tea, milk tea!

279
00:14:05,305 --> 00:14:07,245
Milk tea?! There’s milk?!

280
00:14:07,649 --> 00:14:07,969
Yes!

281
00:14:07,994 --> 00:14:09,948
I’m lactose intolerant,
you monster!

282
00:14:09,973 --> 00:14:11,299
Are you trying to kill me?!

283
00:14:13,007 --> 00:14:14,967
Clinic! Clinic, clinic!

284
00:14:15,886 --> 00:14:16,886
Clinic!

285
00:14:17,332 --> 00:14:18,332
Clinic!

286
00:14:22,771 --> 00:14:24,898
Atasha, are you okay?

287
00:14:25,130 --> 00:14:26,130
I am okay.

288
00:14:26,223 --> 00:14:27,343
No, Tita, she’s not.

289
00:14:27,532 --> 00:14:29,065
What happened?

290
00:14:29,313 --> 00:14:31,662
She’s been in a bad mood since
yesterday… since that Hannah girl.

291
00:14:31,686 --> 00:14:33,092
You know, the
snobby niece of Tso K.

292
00:14:33,117 --> 00:14:33,937
Yes, yes!

293
00:14:33,962 --> 00:14:37,120
Shhh! Someone might hear
you, what are you doing?

294
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,007
Really now?

295
00:14:40,425 --> 00:14:42,985
Didn’t you say yesterday
your blood was boiling?

296
00:14:43,010 --> 00:14:44,305
Let’s just keep it here.

297
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:49,693
You know, I heard what happened.

298
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,914
It was like one of those
Korean dramas I watch.

299
00:14:54,382 --> 00:14:56,995
Honestly, I’m just waiting to
see what happens next, Tash!

300
00:14:57,196 --> 00:14:59,136
Lola, don’t turn it
into a show, please.

301
00:14:59,161 --> 00:15:00,645
Hey, you’re giving
these to us for free, right?

302
00:15:00,669 --> 00:15:03,684
No take backs,
you’ve already said so!

303
00:15:05,252 --> 00:15:06,612
Hi!

304
00:15:10,906 --> 00:15:12,126
Hi!

305
00:15:12,572 --> 00:15:13,812
Do you hear a dog somewhere?

306
00:15:16,264 --> 00:15:17,704
Hi, hello!

307
00:15:17,729 --> 00:15:19,921
Wow! Wow!

308
00:15:20,462 --> 00:15:24,789
So many customers
in your bakery!

309
00:15:25,832 --> 00:15:27,312
Oh, thank you!

310
00:15:27,890 --> 00:15:29,222
But you know what?

311
00:15:29,247 --> 00:15:33,637
Everything they
have, we have too.

312
00:15:33,662 --> 00:15:35,062
Over there, look!
Ours taste better.

313
00:15:35,496 --> 00:15:36,896
- Oh?
- A real bakery?

314
00:15:37,276 --> 00:15:38,276
Yes!

315
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:39,460
Ours is even better.

316
00:15:39,586 --> 00:15:40,826
And look at that! Look!

317
00:15:42,779 --> 00:15:44,332
Wow!

318
00:15:44,357 --> 00:15:45,357
- Wow!
- Half price!

319
00:15:46,244 --> 00:15:47,244
Nice, right?

320
00:15:48,298 --> 00:15:50,058
And cheaper, too.

321
00:15:50,204 --> 00:15:53,064
We’re offering half price
because it’s our grand reopening.

322
00:15:53,089 --> 00:15:55,679
Let’s check it out, let’s check it out!

323
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,985
Hey, dial it down. You
look way too happy.

324
00:15:58,411 --> 00:15:59,864
We’re just checking if it’s legit.

325
00:16:00,044 --> 00:16:01,237
We’re spying for you.

326
00:16:02,221 --> 00:16:05,187
You’re way too
cheerful to be spies.

327
00:16:05,445 --> 00:16:06,745
And you, Hannah…

328
00:16:08,241 --> 00:16:09,763
Tasha, Tasha, come on…

329
00:16:09,788 --> 00:16:10,801
Relax, okay?

330
00:16:12,032 --> 00:16:14,165
You’ve teased me so many times.

331
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:19,999
Once, twice, three times?

332
00:16:20,531 --> 00:16:22,474
How often is “once”?

333
00:16:25,669 --> 00:16:27,402
Why are you mad?

334
00:16:28,082 --> 00:16:30,555
Why does it feel like it’s my fault?

335
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:38,430
Because you’re nothing but a
second-rate, trying-hard, copycat!

336
00:16:41,607 --> 00:16:43,721
The world is one big Quiapo…

337
00:16:43,821 --> 00:16:44,821
Oh!

338
00:16:45,155 --> 00:16:47,088
Full of snatchers.

339
00:16:48,045 --> 00:16:50,472
You’ll get robbed! So fight back!

340
00:16:51,897 --> 00:16:54,071
God is my witness!

341
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:57,437
Your good days are numbered!

342
00:16:57,884 --> 00:17:00,357
Not every law is on your side!

343
00:17:01,009 --> 00:17:08,145
You’ll taste the justice
of the oppressed!

344
00:17:09,163 --> 00:17:10,190
Amazing!

345
00:17:10,215 --> 00:17:11,215
You said it!

346
00:17:11,835 --> 00:17:13,762
You want war?!

347
00:17:14,891 --> 00:17:17,057
I’ll give you war!

348
00:17:17,082 --> 00:17:18,324
Why are they trembling?

349
00:17:18,443 --> 00:17:19,417
Maybe it’s just cold.

350
00:17:19,442 --> 00:17:21,784
Just say the time and place...

351
00:17:21,974 --> 00:17:26,121
I’ll be there with my
red rubber shoes!

352
00:17:30,824 --> 00:17:32,476
Wait! Don’t do it, Tash!

353
00:17:32,870 --> 00:17:33,818
Oh!

354
00:17:33,843 --> 00:17:35,029
Don't do it, Tash!

355
00:17:53,983 --> 00:17:55,443
And we’ve just witnessed

356
00:17:56,604 --> 00:17:59,477
the fierce battle
between rivals.

357
00:18:00,443 --> 00:18:01,763
So intense!

358
00:18:02,384 --> 00:18:06,757
Good thing we got splashed
so it cooled us down.

359
00:18:08,183 --> 00:18:11,543
Let’s all stay tuned
for the next chapter of

360
00:18:12,362 --> 00:18:14,789
Hannah and Tasha!

361
00:18:29,519 --> 00:18:32,112
In fairness, bread is cheaper here.

362
00:18:32,996 --> 00:18:36,062
Yeah, it is, but the ones
from Tash still taste better.

363
00:18:36,099 --> 00:18:36,634
True.

364
00:18:36,659 --> 00:18:37,659
Right?

365
00:18:38,086 --> 00:18:39,086
This one’s tough.

366
00:18:39,336 --> 00:18:40,396
Oh, really?

367
00:18:45,607 --> 00:18:46,607
Well,

368
00:18:47,271 --> 00:18:52,211
I could make ours taste just
as good as their pan de regla,

369
00:18:52,245 --> 00:18:54,600
Spanish bread, and ensaymada

370
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:57,684
if I only knew their recipe.

371
00:18:57,752 --> 00:18:58,612
Ah…

372
00:18:58,637 --> 00:18:59,646
But you don’t know it.

373
00:19:00,452 --> 00:19:02,385
How would you even know, sis,

374
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:05,000
when it’s written in their
bakery’s recipe book?

375
00:19:05,067 --> 00:19:06,067
Oh no,

376
00:19:06,547 --> 00:19:14,201
what if I could sneak a
peek at that recipe book...

377
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:16,303
would you help me out?

378
00:19:18,413 --> 00:19:20,353
And why would we help you, huh?

379
00:19:20,437 --> 00:19:21,764
Tash is our friend.

380
00:19:21,894 --> 00:19:23,741
In fact, we’re here to sp–.

381
00:19:24,238 --> 00:19:25,238
Hey!

382
00:19:26,122 --> 00:19:26,916
What?

383
00:19:26,986 --> 00:19:29,406
- To go to the spa!
- To go to the spa after we eat!

384
00:19:29,431 --> 00:19:31,071
- We’re heading to SpaKarl.
- There, look.

385
00:19:31,329 --> 00:19:33,603
So wait, you’re really friends?

386
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,767
Yes, BFFs!

387
00:19:34,804 --> 00:19:35,750
Sometimes, depending
on the season.

388
00:19:35,781 --> 00:19:38,087
Wow, you’re such sweet friends.

389
00:19:38,121 --> 00:19:39,121
Super!

390
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,240
But you know…

391
00:19:41,488 --> 00:19:44,455
how can you even
say you’re her friends

392
00:19:44,494 --> 00:19:48,694
when she makes you pay
every time you eat there?

393
00:19:49,975 --> 00:19:51,135
You’ve got a point, girl.

394
00:19:51,266 --> 00:19:52,426
That made me think, actually.

395
00:19:53,174 --> 00:19:54,414
Are we on the dark side now?

396
00:19:54,458 --> 00:19:56,998
Wait, I’ve got an idea!

397
00:19:57,038 --> 00:19:58,038
What?

398
00:20:00,436 --> 00:20:03,036
If you give me –

399
00:20:03,158 --> 00:20:06,924
even just show
me – their recipe,

400
00:20:08,816 --> 00:20:10,809
you get free food here forever!

401
00:20:12,529 --> 00:20:13,381
Free?!

402
00:20:13,406 --> 00:20:15,310
Girl, what do you want,
soft copy or hard copy?

403
00:20:15,335 --> 00:20:17,628
Andres, Atasha,

404
00:20:18,065 --> 00:20:20,354
if you keep frowning like that,

405
00:20:20,379 --> 00:20:22,911
we’re not going to get any customers!

406
00:20:22,946 --> 00:20:24,786
Look at your faces!

407
00:20:27,709 --> 00:20:29,669
- It’s because of Hannah–
- Yeah, it’s Ate Hannah!

408
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,580
Right? Same!

409
00:20:31,625 --> 00:20:35,726
I’m getting pissed at her too, she’s
stealing all our customers, Mom!

410
00:20:35,751 --> 00:20:36,150
What?!

411
00:20:36,175 --> 00:20:39,089
Yeah, Mom! And she’s
even blocking me and Anne!

412
00:20:39,114 --> 00:20:40,114
So what now?!

413
00:20:40,369 --> 00:20:41,294
What?!

414
00:20:41,319 --> 00:20:43,538
What’s going on th–

415
00:20:43,717 --> 00:20:45,215
my love, did you know about this?!

416
00:20:46,596 --> 00:20:47,596
Hold on a second.

417
00:20:47,829 --> 00:20:48,829
You two

418
00:20:49,590 --> 00:20:51,703
should just give them
some time to adjust.

419
00:20:52,116 --> 00:20:54,969
You’re the ones who
should adjust for now.

420
00:20:55,018 --> 00:20:56,784
Just like with Tso K.

421
00:20:56,910 --> 00:20:59,436
You saw how angry
he used to be at me,

422
00:20:59,461 --> 00:21:00,394
we were enemies.

423
00:21:00,419 --> 00:21:06,547
. But I let it go, and
now look – we’re BFFs.

424
00:21:07,032 --> 00:21:11,324
Right? So just chill.
Relax and let it be for now.

425
00:21:11,804 --> 00:21:13,530
Well, you’ve got a point.

426
00:21:13,694 --> 00:21:15,981
- Right? Just let it go.
- You’re right, my love.

427
00:21:16,023 --> 00:21:17,023
Yeah.

428
00:21:17,066 --> 00:21:19,173
Okay then, Atasha, Andres,

429
00:21:19,449 --> 00:21:22,546
let’s head inside and fix up.

430
00:21:22,571 --> 00:21:24,825
And my love, you stay
here and keep watch.

431
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:25,909
Me again?

432
00:21:26,062 --> 00:21:27,102
Why is it always me?

433
00:21:27,127 --> 00:21:29,554
Of course! You’ve got this.

434
00:21:30,034 --> 00:21:31,760
You always leave me behind.

435
00:21:33,448 --> 00:21:34,015
Come on!

436
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:37,305
Alright, I got this.
Go help your mom.

437
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:38,738
See you later, my love!

438
00:21:46,321 --> 00:21:48,548
Hey, Tso K!

439
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:49,589
BFF!

440
00:21:49,614 --> 00:21:52,108
Don’t go calling
me BFF like that!

441
00:21:53,668 --> 00:21:55,702
Why are you so
hot-headed again?!

442
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:57,297
Why are you mad at me now?

443
00:21:57,565 --> 00:21:58,820
I talked to Hannah!

444
00:21:58,859 --> 00:21:59,564
And?

445
00:21:59,602 --> 00:22:02,116
When I talked to her,
everything came flooding back!

446
00:22:02,301 --> 00:22:03,115
What came back?!

447
00:22:03,140 --> 00:22:05,357
The memories of how you
stole everything from me.

448
00:22:05,922 --> 00:22:06,962
You stole it!

449
00:22:06,987 --> 00:22:08,653
Are we really doing this again?

450
00:22:08,687 --> 00:22:10,300
BFF, that was so long ago.

451
00:22:10,713 --> 00:22:13,246
Cha and I have two kids now. Right?

452
00:22:14,090 --> 00:22:15,090
Even so!

453
00:22:15,153 --> 00:22:17,447
Of course I remember all
the awful things you did to me.

454
00:22:17,472 --> 00:22:18,950
Stop it – just relax!

455
00:22:18,981 --> 00:22:19,995
You can’t treat me like that!

456
00:22:20,019 --> 00:22:21,865
Stop it – I’ll just
give you a massage!

457
00:22:21,890 --> 00:22:25,000
- You can’t just…
- Calm down…

458
00:22:25,025 --> 00:22:26,545
…treat me like that.

459
00:22:26,570 --> 00:22:27,950
Don’t lose your temper.

460
00:22:27,981 --> 00:22:31,038
Oh no! No way! I’m really mad!

461
00:22:31,063 --> 00:22:32,677
Nope, here – I’ve
got you. There!

462
00:22:32,702 --> 00:22:34,442
You can’t do that to me.

463
00:22:35,379 --> 00:22:36,039
There, okay?

464
00:22:36,385 --> 00:22:37,572
That actually feels okay.

465
00:22:39,616 --> 00:22:40,895
Anywhere else that hurts?

466
00:22:41,482 --> 00:22:43,191
Here, here!

467
00:22:43,216 --> 00:22:44,231
There!

468
00:22:45,659 --> 00:22:47,840
I love you, I love you, BFF!

469
00:22:47,865 --> 00:22:49,292
I love you too!

470
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:53,474
Kuya Aga, can I buy
some ensaymada?

471
00:22:53,615 --> 00:22:55,988
You, seriously?

472
00:22:56,403 --> 00:22:58,570
You always ruin the
moment with your timing!

473
00:22:58,834 --> 00:23:02,594
I was right there, it was
getting good, now go away.

474
00:23:02,979 --> 00:23:05,072
If you don’t leave,
I’ll knock you down.

475
00:23:05,225 --> 00:23:06,225
Get out of here!

476
00:23:06,562 --> 00:23:07,649
I’ll hurt you.

477
00:23:08,226 --> 00:23:09,326
I was right there!

478
00:23:09,519 --> 00:23:11,032
You’re shooing away my customer?

479
00:23:11,057 --> 00:23:13,036
BFF… I’m seriously pissed.

480
00:23:13,418 --> 00:23:15,786
My love, my love! My love, my love!

481
00:23:15,979 --> 00:23:16,893
You too?!

482
00:23:16,932 --> 00:23:17,806
What now?

483
00:23:17,890 --> 00:23:20,084
That makes two of me…
so now there’s three of us.

484
00:23:20,111 --> 00:23:20,664
What?

485
00:23:20,689 --> 00:23:22,151
I’m just so annoyed
with this guy!

486
00:23:22,306 --> 00:23:25,904
I’ve been trying to cool off, but I can’t.

487
00:23:25,929 --> 00:23:26,982
I’m so mad at him.

488
00:23:27,015 --> 00:23:29,461
I was just giving him a
massage because he was angry.

489
00:23:29,486 --> 00:23:31,119
You two look way too close.

490
00:23:31,210 --> 00:23:32,324
Me? Close with him?

491
00:23:32,349 --> 00:23:33,069
Yes!

492
00:23:33,094 --> 00:23:36,484
I’ll kick him if I have to.
He’s testing my patience.

493
00:23:37,575 --> 00:23:38,022
Why?

494
00:23:38,064 --> 00:23:40,344
Ah, my love, can you help us?

495
00:23:40,441 --> 00:23:42,054
- We need your muscles.
- Sure.

496
00:23:42,089 --> 00:23:44,124
Hold on, hold on. Just wait. I’ll leave
you here for now. Huh? Wait a sec!

497
00:23:44,148 --> 00:23:45,675
Huh? Wait a sec!

498
00:23:46,863 --> 00:23:48,003
Just wait, Tso K, okay?

499
00:23:48,545 --> 00:23:49,366
Bye, Tso K!

500
00:23:49,406 --> 00:23:50,500
Don’t stay mad!

501
00:23:50,919 --> 00:23:53,793
I wasn’t done! That felt good!

502
00:23:54,801 --> 00:23:57,568
My back hurts!

503
00:23:58,113 --> 00:24:00,906
Ash is so bossy!

504
00:24:00,966 --> 00:24:04,026
I only met her today… I mean, Tash.

505
00:24:04,086 --> 00:24:06,593
Wow, you’re so tired
you forgot her name?

506
00:24:08,154 --> 00:24:10,974
You know, I have an idea
– since we’re already here,

507
00:24:11,326 --> 00:24:14,530
we should be de-stressing, right?

508
00:24:15,219 --> 00:24:16,359
This looks nice!

509
00:24:16,384 --> 00:24:17,887
Let’s go? Let’s go!

510
00:24:17,912 --> 00:24:18,912
Game!

511
00:24:20,949 --> 00:24:25,539
Hey! Oh! Hello!

512
00:24:25,572 --> 00:24:26,271
Hi!

513
00:24:26,296 --> 00:24:27,605
Wait, never mind. Let’s
not. Let’s just go home.

514
00:24:27,629 --> 00:24:28,629
This is solid, boss!

515
00:24:29,275 --> 00:24:34,128
So, um… will your stress go away

516
00:24:34,182 --> 00:24:38,136
if we let our new massage
therapists work on you?

517
00:24:38,161 --> 00:24:39,610
Cherry, Apple!

518
00:24:39,821 --> 00:24:41,181
Boss, they’re great!

519
00:24:44,541 --> 00:24:47,608
Cherry, Apple? No watermelon?

520
00:24:47,749 --> 00:24:50,849
Oh, we can have one. On one condition.

521
00:24:51,261 --> 00:24:52,482
What condition?

522
00:24:53,063 --> 00:24:54,063
Uh…

523
00:24:58,257 --> 00:25:01,824
we need someone to
manage our Bake K shop.

524
00:25:02,119 --> 00:25:04,412
Maybe you could transfer
there? Just move over!

525
00:25:04,609 --> 00:25:09,576
Huh? Transfer? No way! Not
happening, we don’t want to!

526
00:25:11,994 --> 00:25:15,214
Oh, you don’t have to answer now.

527
00:25:15,419 --> 00:25:17,832
Just think about it first,
come on, just think about it.

528
00:25:17,857 --> 00:25:19,016
Think about it?

529
00:25:19,041 --> 00:25:21,556
Come on, come on. While
the girls sit on your lap.

530
00:25:21,581 --> 00:25:22,688
Huh?

531
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:25,158
Sit on our lap? Are you sure?

532
00:25:25,183 --> 00:25:26,296
Yes, lap and all.

533
00:25:26,609 --> 00:25:27,609
There!

534
00:25:28,773 --> 00:25:30,286
You seem to really like this, Je!

535
00:25:30,499 --> 00:25:31,246
I do.

536
00:25:31,271 --> 00:25:32,003
You’re enjoying this, huh?

537
00:25:32,028 --> 00:25:33,675
Yeah, you know, stuff like
this doesn’t happen often.

538
00:25:33,699 --> 00:25:34,841
Oh, you like that?

539
00:25:34,866 --> 00:25:38,219
No… uh… I don’t. I don’t even
want to go home anymore.

540
00:25:38,244 --> 00:25:39,244
Huh?

541
00:25:39,366 --> 00:25:40,867
I don’t want to go home –
someone might get mad.

542
00:25:40,891 --> 00:25:43,421
Nope, no one’s gonna get
mad. Here, hold on to that.

543
00:25:43,476 --> 00:25:45,029
You think you’ll still make it home?

544
00:25:45,096 --> 00:25:46,096
There you go.

545
00:25:46,194 --> 00:25:47,974
We already took a
photo of the recipe book

546
00:25:48,006 --> 00:25:50,221
with the instructions on
how to make ensaymada.

547
00:25:50,593 --> 00:25:52,389
We sent it to you
already, girl, okay?

548
00:25:53,013 --> 00:25:54,013
Fine!

549
00:25:54,064 --> 00:25:56,423
Hey, Hannah, don’t
forget our free food, okay?

550
00:25:56,629 --> 00:25:58,009
Yeah, yeah!

551
00:25:58,143 --> 00:25:59,096
Promise, okay?

552
00:25:59,121 --> 00:26:00,325
You said it!

553
00:26:02,861 --> 00:26:05,327
Hannah, seriously,
don’t forget. If you forget...

554
00:26:05,352 --> 00:26:06,486
I won’t forget, come on.

555
00:26:06,511 --> 00:26:09,525
You…what’s going on here?

556
00:26:24,437 --> 00:26:27,990
Let’s see who wins this one.

557
00:26:28,056 --> 00:26:29,148
Nothing.

558
00:26:29,562 --> 00:26:32,802
Why? Are you the only one
allowed to make friends here?

559
00:26:32,922 --> 00:26:33,922
No.

560
00:26:34,097 --> 00:26:34,749
Huh?

561
00:26:34,774 --> 00:26:36,774
I’m the only one
who’s going to win here.

562
00:26:38,284 --> 00:26:44,437
Oh, you wish! I can
beat you at anything.

563
00:26:44,462 --> 00:26:46,922
Alright, let’s go
with tongue twisters.

564
00:26:50,063 --> 00:26:51,063
Hello!

565
00:26:51,456 --> 00:26:52,496
How is everybody doing?

566
00:26:52,521 --> 00:26:54,955
Welcome to the mega
tongue twister challenge

567
00:26:55,261 --> 00:26:58,308
between Hannah and Tasha!

568
00:26:58,333 --> 00:26:59,647
Let’s hear some applause!

569
00:27:03,132 --> 00:27:07,319
Three…two…one!

570
00:27:07,717 --> 00:27:08,770
Fight!

571
00:27:09,027 --> 00:27:10,561
Siopao, siomai, suman!

572
00:27:11,933 --> 00:27:12,734
Here, here.

573
00:27:12,759 --> 00:27:14,659
Okay, okay, game, game, game.

574
00:27:15,013 --> 00:27:17,921
Seventy-seven silly white sharks!

575
00:27:21,513 --> 00:27:23,821
- Wait, wait, wait, wait!
- Oh, oh, go on!

576
00:27:23,846 --> 00:27:26,510
Susan stuffed the small
silo with silly soft chicks.

577
00:27:29,267 --> 00:27:33,056
She sells seashells by the seashore!

578
00:27:38,099 --> 00:27:39,459
You’re really
getting on my nerves!

579
00:27:39,636 --> 00:27:41,051
Oh, oh, oh, oh!

580
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,796
Girl you’ve got no one
on your side anymore!

581
00:27:44,271 --> 00:27:45,271
Direk!

582
00:27:46,987 --> 00:27:50,562
A peck of pickled pepper, Peter Piper
picked. If Peter Piper picked a peck

583
00:27:50,587 --> 00:27:53,827
of pickled pepper, where is the peck
of pickled pepper Peter Piper picked?

584
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:58,967
Okay, now we’re
going back to Tagalog!

585
00:27:59,005 --> 00:27:59,504
What?!

586
00:27:59,529 --> 00:28:01,506
Leroy’s wrist watch is –!

587
00:28:01,575 --> 00:28:02,575
Oh!

588
00:28:04,780 --> 00:28:06,200
Well then, Leroy is rich!

589
00:28:06,306 --> 00:28:07,913
Yeah!

590
00:28:08,256 --> 00:28:10,303
Alright! Round closed!

591
00:28:11,489 --> 00:28:12,489
I smell!

592
00:28:13,424 --> 00:28:16,544
And with that, you’ve
witnessed a very intense battle.

593
00:28:16,737 --> 00:28:17,697
Who will…

594
00:28:17,722 --> 00:28:21,234
let’s give a round of applause for Tasha!

595
00:28:22,883 --> 00:28:25,000
And for Hannah!

596
00:28:26,571 --> 00:28:28,671
Who will win in the debate
between these two ladies?

597
00:28:28,696 --> 00:28:31,026
Who’s got the
caliber—or the danger?

598
00:28:31,051 --> 00:28:36,091
Find out in the next Mega Tongue
Twister, let’s hear that applause!

599
00:28:42,153 --> 00:28:47,541
Anne, head inside for a
bit. I need to talk to Andres.

600
00:28:48,525 --> 00:28:49,525
Alright, Ate.

601
00:29:01,639 --> 00:29:03,600
Boy, how much are you?

602
00:29:03,625 --> 00:29:04,775
I’m not an escort, okay?

603
00:29:05,106 --> 00:29:06,519
That’s not what I meant.

604
00:29:07,061 --> 00:29:10,527
How much for you to
stay away from my sister?

605
00:29:26,071 --> 00:29:28,518
You know, that’s not enough.

606
00:29:28,799 --> 00:29:31,332
Add two more zeroes.

607
00:29:34,274 --> 00:29:35,274
There, is that okay now?

608
00:29:35,669 --> 00:29:37,282
You know what, one more.

609
00:29:38,064 --> 00:29:39,064
One more?

610
00:29:41,744 --> 00:29:43,301
This kid is all about the money.

611
00:29:49,431 --> 00:29:50,431
That’ll do.

612
00:29:52,310 --> 00:29:53,310
That’ll do?

613
00:29:53,335 --> 00:29:55,298
That’ll do to blow my nose on!

614
00:29:57,762 --> 00:29:58,757
Hey!

615
00:30:00,759 --> 00:30:02,047
You know, Hannah,

616
00:30:02,209 --> 00:30:05,074
no amount of money
in the world can match

617
00:30:05,099 --> 00:30:07,053
what it feels like to
be Anne’s boyfriend,

618
00:30:07,483 --> 00:30:08,743
so you can keep your money.

619
00:30:09,674 --> 00:30:10,674
I’m loyal.

620
00:30:12,875 --> 00:30:15,834
Alright, good.

621
00:30:15,859 --> 00:30:18,085
In that case, I’m okay with it.

622
00:30:18,110 --> 00:30:19,497
Huh? Really?

623
00:30:19,910 --> 00:30:21,215
- Okay!
- Really?!

624
00:30:22,054 --> 00:30:23,054
Hey! Hey!

625
00:30:26,213 --> 00:30:28,659
Just don’t ever
make my sister cry,

626
00:30:28,684 --> 00:30:30,117
or I’ll be the one
making you cry.

627
00:30:30,148 --> 00:30:31,666
No, no. Of course not.

628
00:30:31,881 --> 00:30:32,881
You better not, okay?

629
00:30:33,189 --> 00:30:34,489
Wow!

630
00:30:35,606 --> 00:30:37,899
We really practiced
that for a long time! x.

631
00:30:37,924 --> 00:30:38,723
Hey, that wasn’t free, you know?

632
00:30:38,748 --> 00:30:39,634
Huh?

633
00:30:39,659 --> 00:30:40,702
Come on, girl, put it back.

634
00:30:40,726 --> 00:30:43,359
Hey, no, you guys
should pay, right?

635
00:30:43,384 --> 00:30:44,384
You said it was free.

636
00:30:44,817 --> 00:30:46,020
I thought we were friends.

637
00:30:46,045 --> 00:30:47,179
We are friends.

638
00:30:47,244 --> 00:30:52,614
[background chattering]

639
00:30:52,639 --> 00:30:54,118
Hi!

640
00:30:54,204 --> 00:30:55,550
[chattering]

641
00:30:57,253 --> 00:30:58,253
Ehem!

642
00:30:59,230 --> 00:31:01,064
Hi!

643
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:07,299
I know you keep coming back
because their ensaymada is good,

644
00:31:07,509 --> 00:31:10,863
but ours is cheaper!

645
00:31:11,202 --> 00:31:13,035
And not only that,

646
00:31:13,432 --> 00:31:15,334
it tastes the same!

647
00:31:15,359 --> 00:31:16,827
And guess what, guys?

648
00:31:18,655 --> 00:31:21,668
Half price on all
breads and pastries!

649
00:31:21,885 --> 00:31:26,531
Bake K Naman grand reopening!

650
00:31:26,556 --> 00:31:27,884
Give it a try, come on!

651
00:31:28,648 --> 00:31:30,161
Alright, fine.

652
00:31:35,122 --> 00:31:36,242
Pwe!

653
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,021
It doesn’t even taste the same!

654
00:31:39,241 --> 00:31:40,381
It got worse!

655
00:31:42,446 --> 00:31:43,479
That’s fake news!

656
00:31:43,636 --> 00:31:45,432
I don’t believe you. You, try it.

657
00:31:50,193 --> 00:31:52,850
Pwe! It really doesn’t taste
the same, it got worse!

658
00:31:53,114 --> 00:31:54,334
That’s impossible!

659
00:31:54,587 --> 00:31:56,786
Impossible that it doesn’t taste
the same—and it’s delicious!

660
00:31:56,810 --> 00:31:59,044
I got the recipe, it was from friends.

661
00:31:59,069 --> 00:32:00,509
That was the… that
was the right one!

662
00:32:02,142 --> 00:32:03,796
It’s a prank!

663
00:32:03,821 --> 00:32:05,095
Sorry, okay?

664
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:07,466
But they told me
about your plan.

665
00:32:08,217 --> 00:32:10,321
We gave you a fake recipe.

666
00:32:18,524 --> 00:32:20,000
Oh, is that so?

667
00:32:21,766 --> 00:32:24,689
Let’s see if your
employees are trustworthy.

668
00:32:24,714 --> 00:32:26,014
They’re transferring to us.

669
00:32:27,502 --> 00:32:30,435
We already told Tash your plan.

670
00:32:30,689 --> 00:32:33,849
Even if your offer’s
good, we’re not leaving.

671
00:32:34,243 --> 00:32:35,243
Never!

672
00:32:35,268 --> 00:32:36,268
That’s true.

673
00:32:37,468 --> 00:32:38,728
This cousin of ours...

674
00:32:39,476 --> 00:32:40,963
even if she’s strict with us...

675
00:32:42,096 --> 00:32:43,096
she loves us.

676
00:32:43,124 --> 00:32:44,124
Unlike you.

677
00:32:44,784 --> 00:32:45,784
You’re mean.

678
00:32:46,399 --> 00:32:47,399
And you know what,

679
00:32:47,761 --> 00:32:49,491
I was actually starting to like you.

680
00:32:49,928 --> 00:32:52,061
But you turned out to be mean.

681
00:32:52,643 --> 00:32:55,063
I even imagined us falling in love,

682
00:32:55,336 --> 00:32:56,662
then you’d love me back,

683
00:32:57,057 --> 00:33:00,070
then I pictured
us getting married!

684
00:33:01,180 --> 00:33:03,107
But now—forget it!

685
00:33:03,457 --> 00:33:07,643
That’s cancelled! I’m done.

686
00:33:09,331 --> 00:33:10,571
See that, Hannah?

687
00:33:11,238 --> 00:33:13,664
Ensaymada isn’t just
the investment here.

688
00:33:15,203 --> 00:33:16,803
We invest in trustworthy
friendship, too.

689
00:33:17,038 --> 00:33:20,306
Remember this—loyalty…

690
00:33:25,782 --> 00:33:32,110
And that’s how the feud
between Hannah and Tasha ends.

691
00:33:32,410 --> 00:33:35,903
And our heroine wins. Applause!

692
00:33:46,820 --> 00:33:48,180
You’re bad, huh?

693
00:33:50,803 --> 00:33:51,803
Alright then.

694
00:33:52,756 --> 00:33:53,756
Bring it on!

695
00:34:07,916 --> 00:34:08,916
My beloved niece,

696
00:34:11,246 --> 00:34:12,952
I heard what happened earlier.

697
00:34:15,775 --> 00:34:17,275
You shouldn’t have done that.

698
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:26,677
Actually, I was just testing them.

699
00:34:27,198 --> 00:34:29,772
Tso K, the way you used to talk

700
00:34:29,829 --> 00:34:31,835
about Uncle Aga before—so extra.

701
00:34:32,465 --> 00:34:35,725
So I assumed their
kids would be the same.

702
00:34:36,779 --> 00:34:38,666
But they turned out okay.

703
00:34:40,102 --> 00:34:41,102
Come here, nephew.

704
00:34:45,514 --> 00:34:46,514
You know,

705
00:34:48,581 --> 00:34:50,295
I used to be like you.

706
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,280
I was the same way.

707
00:34:53,628 --> 00:34:56,135
The people here in
the barangay are kind.

708
00:34:56,818 --> 00:35:00,598
Tso K, I’m just looking out for you.

709
00:35:01,746 --> 00:35:04,232
You know you’re my
favorite uncle, right?

710
00:35:09,471 --> 00:35:11,557
Well? Got something to say?

711
00:35:13,099 --> 00:35:16,480
Tso, she started it!

712
00:35:19,674 --> 00:35:21,000
- Me?
- Come on, just go first!

713
00:35:21,087 --> 00:35:22,707
She’s the one with
the shady moves!

714
00:35:29,197 --> 00:35:30,197
Sorry, Tash…

715
00:35:30,811 --> 00:35:31,811
Hey…

716
00:35:32,986 --> 00:35:34,153
Sorry, Tash.

717
00:35:35,695 --> 00:35:36,695
It’s okay.

718
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:40,675
I actually enjoyed the
competition part. Hug it out!

719
00:35:41,936 --> 00:35:44,356
Aww! That’s a hug moment!

720
00:35:44,381 --> 00:35:45,947
Come on, hug it out!

721
00:35:56,102 --> 00:35:59,118
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

722
00:36:00,425 --> 00:36:01,965
So you actually
liked the competition?

723
00:36:02,537 --> 00:36:03,537
Right?

724
00:36:03,692 --> 00:36:05,286
But don’t you have
a bakery to manage?

725
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:09,905
I’m sorry, darling.

726
00:36:10,513 --> 00:36:11,513
Ooh…

727
00:36:12,017 --> 00:36:13,170
But it’s not over yet.

728
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:19,146
May the best businesswoman win.

729
00:36:19,943 --> 00:36:21,450
Whoa!

730
00:36:22,391 --> 00:36:24,085
Looks like the
drama’s not over yet!

731
00:36:24,395 --> 00:36:28,500
Stay tuned for book two slash
season two of Hannah versus Tasha!

732
00:36:28,531 --> 00:36:30,098
Let’s give them a
round of applause!

733
00:36:32,526 --> 00:36:33,783
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

734
00:36:34,326 --> 00:36:36,982
If it were up to me, I’d
go for a slap showdown!

735
00:36:37,831 --> 00:36:38,831
A slap showdown?!

736
00:36:39,204 --> 00:36:41,424
Just to relieve the tension in the body.

737
00:36:42,188 --> 00:36:43,308
Like this...

738
00:36:46,131 --> 00:36:48,538
That really stings...

739
00:36:51,438 --> 00:36:53,085
Well, it did release
some tension!

740
00:36:53,469 --> 00:36:55,477
What was that?!

741
00:36:56,372 --> 00:37:01,938
Hold on, who keeps playing the
dramatic music?!

742
00:37:02,413 --> 00:37:03,393
That hair’s so thin!

743
00:37:03,418 --> 00:37:06,308
Oh, it’s you?! So it
was you all along! Tso K!

744
00:37:07,005 --> 00:37:08,632
- So it was you all along!
- Tso K!

745
00:37:08,657 --> 00:37:09,657
Oh!

746
00:37:09,931 --> 00:37:12,284
Don’t take the law
into your own hands!

747
00:37:13,472 --> 00:37:14,472
I got this!

748
00:37:25,614 --> 00:37:28,695
That therapist is so handsome!

749
00:37:28,734 --> 00:37:30,463
Oh my gosh, beshy!
Let’s make this go viral!

750
00:37:31,806 --> 00:37:32,754
Andres!

751
00:37:32,779 --> 00:37:34,626
I can’t hear you!

752
00:37:34,651 --> 00:37:35,861
I’m just going home!

753
00:37:35,886 --> 00:37:38,840
We’re going to win
the family’s trust.

754
00:37:38,865 --> 00:37:42,430
Once we have that… BOOM!

755
00:37:42,455 --> 00:37:47,611
What kind of scheme is
Hannah cooking up this time?

756
00:37:47,636 --> 00:37:50,725
I want to be part of your family.

757
00:37:50,947 --> 00:37:52,720
Go team up with that Hannah!

758
00:37:52,745 --> 00:37:53,745
Tash!
